WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Your history is scattered across years of checkups and different files.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.960
When you need one old result, the search starts again.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.860
Modus brings that history together.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.180
Each satellite opens a file, its readings, and the original evidence.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.327
Ask, when did I last have blood pressure of one hundred?

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.560
Modus asks which number you mean.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:24.870
Choose the top number, and it finds May fourth, twenty sixteen.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.880
Open the source: one hundred over seventy.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.380
The answer comes with its date and original evidence.

00:00:31.913 --> 00:00:33.043
Now add a new report.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:38.643
Muse Spark reads the image, verifies proposed evidence, and checks for missing rows.

00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:43.983
Here it found all three rows, but left the header date and specimen for review.

00:00:44.593 --> 00:00:47.183
I confirm those from the original before saving.

00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:49.443
The source-check warning remains visible.

00:00:49.823 --> 00:00:51.733
Compare it with an earlier checkup.

00:00:51.943 --> 00:00:55.833
Muse inspects the selected reports, then follows related records.

00:00:55.843 --> 00:00:59.338
Two earlier copies both say five point six.

00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:02.953
One says H P L C; the other says immunoassay.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.553
The value matches, but the recorded methods disagree.

00:01:06.943 --> 00:01:09.593
That difference was hidden behind the same number.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:12.693
Open the finding and both sources are right here.

00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:16.173
Modus keeps the disagreement visible, without choosing a winner.

00:01:16.423 --> 00:01:19.933
If the context is uncertain, it withholds a numerical comparison.

00:01:20.643 --> 00:01:24.733
Muse can investigate through bounded tools, but it cannot rewrite your record.

00:01:24.733 --> 00:01:26.653
Corrections need your review.

00:01:27.043 --> 00:01:30.273
Confirm the exact change, then save a new version.

00:01:30.903 --> 00:01:34.893
The previous explanation becomes stale and asks for a refresh.

00:01:35.343 --> 00:01:40.073
Your original file, its printed wording, and the earlier saved version remain available.

00:01:40.443 --> 00:01:42.913
You can correct your history without losing its evidence.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.530
A report can also arrive years late.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.570
This result is dated twenty nineteen, but its file arrived in twenty twenty-six.

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.330
Today's history includes it.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:58.010
Replay what was available in twenty twenty-five, and it stays outside that view.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.270
New evidence does not rewrite what was known then.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.120
Muse reads and investigates.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:08.440
Typed tools check comparisons and bind findings to exact records and versions.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.680
Human-reviewed transactions control every save.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:16.300
Encrypted local storage preserves originals, revisions, and both dates.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:23.820
This is record integrity: answers you can inspect, corrections you can trace, and history you can replay.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:31.100
On fourteen authored three-report cases with real Muse calls, revised comparison rules caught all nine expected

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.040
discrepancies, with zero false flags.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:39.440
These are development results on the same inspected cases, not independent accuracy.

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.060
Export a reviewed summary with its sources.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:46.081
Modus Records: your history, with the original beside it.
